## ST mechanism attribution correction

The final implementation records an ST charging opportunity only when the
current highest-priority ready job is individually unaffordable in the current
decision. An existing charging-hold state, a non-full battery, or an
unaffordable SYNC batch is not sufficient.

Exact affordability (`required == available`) does not count as an ST charging
opportunity. For ST-SYNC, an individually affordable head with an unaffordable
batch remains a SYNC batch-rejection event and is not attributed to ST charging.

This correction changes observability attribution only. Scheduler selection,
dispatch, battery, completion, and deadline behavior remain unchanged.

